name: Partner settlement
tagline: "Agreement-aware partner statement settlement - effective-dated terms, a cycle calendar, statement integrity and a per-agreement compare, over a synthetic corpus"
description: "A partner / wholesale settlement content pack (slices S1 to S6 of the plan: References, statement ingestion, the compare, netting positions with a roll-forward, disputes as Cases, and aging with accruals). Four Reference feeds (partners, effective-dated settlement agreements, daily FX rates, public holidays), a partner statement feed (versioned lines with control totals), a finance payment feed (payments, credit and debit notes) and a stand-in re-rated usage feed that implements the contract the re-rating pack will fill. Twelve chained sql.template Jobs: a settlement-cycle calendar (statement due, dispute window and payment due dates rolled to business days), the current statement lines (re-sends counted once, the highest version wins), statement integrity findings (control total mismatch, duplicate, restated, unknown partner, unknown agreement), our expected amounts and the partner's billed amounts at one grain in the settlement currency, and the settlement findings (amount mismatch, cut-off difference, FX difference, missing statement, unrated usage, missing FX rate), the dispute lines (every amount mismatch and FX difference keyed to its partner and cycle, with the contractual dispute window end); then every money movement at line level with both currencies and the FX row that converted it, a settlement position per netting group and cycle month (payable, receivable, net, the net in each original currency, and the disputed amount beside the net) and a roll-forward (opening + invoiced - paid + adjustments = closing, one row for every month so a quiet month carries the balance); then the aging per agreement and statement cycle (finance records applied oldest cycle first, the open balance and open disputed amount by age bucket, 0-30, 31-60, 61-90, 90+ days by default, and the payment due date) and the accruals per agreement and cycle (our expected amount while no statement has arrived, unbilled before the statement due date and statement_late after it, plus a provision on the disputed amount, default 100 percent). Per-agreement tolerance, FX and cut-off come from the agreement Reference through the SQL; two Reconciliations (voice, SMS) compare the normalised Datasets at exact tolerance 0 and supply the Break lifecycle and Incidents. One Alert Rule fires once per agreement; two more raise one Incident per dispute line and one per partner cycle whose dispute window is about to close, and a Case Rule groups them into one dispute Case per partner and cycle. A fourth Alert Rule names every cycle with an open balance at or past its payment due lead time. Three KPIs (open disputed amount, open balance aged over 60 days, accrued unbilled) and the settlement_overview dashboard show the state. The dispute workflow (OPEN, INVESTIGATING, DISPUTED, AGREED or REJECTED, CREDIT_PENDING, CLOSED), its SLA Policy and its Escalation Rule ship as bodies an administrator applies through their own routes (config/governance/): a Space Template carries no governance. It nets inside one currency, its KPI tiles count one currency (kpi_currency, default USD), and it does not post payments, ledger entries or accruals, and it fetches no market FX rate. Every feed format is synthetic: no real partner statement has been seen. Needs the Standard, Advanced or Preview edition. Runbook: config/runbooks/partner-settlement-runbooks.md."
minEdition: standard
requiresModules[2]: case-management,ops
icon: heroicons_outline:arrows-right-left
contents[10]: "7 Pipelines + canonical schemas (4 References, the statement feed, the finance payment feed, the stand-in re-rated usage feed)", "12 chained sql.template Jobs (calendar, current statements, statement integrity, expected, billed, findings, dispute lines, movements, position, roll-forward, aging, accruals)", "2 Reconciliations (voice, SMS) with their recon.run Jobs", "4 Alert Rules (one Alert per agreement, one Incident per dispute line, one per closing dispute window, one Alert per cycle whose payment is due)", "1 Case Rule and its caserule.evaluate Job (one dispute Case per partner and cycle)", "The dispute workflow, SLA Policy and Escalation Rule as bodies for an administrator to apply", "19 Datasets (7 feeds, 12 Job-written)", "3 KPIs, 6 Widgets and the settlement_overview dashboard", "Zero-row schema seeds", "Runbook"
